title: Extend diff view
pid: 2d1738f1-bf13-46e2-bdf8-9002a7de5fb3
body: |2-
    - Request: =((request . "extend diff view") (view-id . "VIEW_ID"))=,
      where VIEW_ID names a buffer of the diff view. The client
      sends it only for a buffer with no unsaved changes, since the
      server works on the viewforest it registered at the last rerender.
    - Response: LP response-type "extend-diff-view", then a rerender
      stream (rerender-lock, rerender-view*, rerender-done). The
      response is one of:
      - =((processed-summary ...) (errors ()) (warnings ()))=, the save
        response's form, for the buffer as rerendered; the rerender
        stream carries that buffer.
      - =((errors ("REFUSAL")) (warnings ()))= when the
        connection has a skgrepo restriction, VIEW_ID is not a buffer of the
        diff view, or the rerender fails. The rerender stream is empty.
    - Logic: the graph straddle is brought up to date, and the buffer's
      pruned change view sets recomputed. Each node of U without an editable
      occurrence becomes editable at its first content occurrence in
      level order, its children claiming as the buffer read back would; a
      node shown only as a write-protected folder member counts as shown
      nowhere, since the extension makes no folder member editable (an
      editable-view request, C-c s e, can, and its node then counts as
      shown there). The buffer
      then gains, as roots at the end in ID order, the origins of D it
      makes editable nowhere; R is deduplicated with the buffer's roots
      pinned, so that a changed cycle that already has a root gains no
      second one. Last, the buffer is refreshed once, as after a save,
      which gives each node made editable its body and draws its content
      list and the content of each appended root.
      =server/serve/handlers/extend_diff_view.rs=, =server/diff_view/buffer_rerender.rs=
      ('ensure_editableOccurrences_exist',
      'contentOrigins_missing_from_buffer'), and 'refresh_view' in
      =server/rerender_pass.rs=.
